    "chunk_text": "1AI \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3: (I) \u0dd9\u0da1\u0daf\u0dba \u2013 \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba \u2013 2025.07.17PART I: SEC. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 17.07.2025\n\n\u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba\n\n\u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2The Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\n\u0d85\u0d82\u0d9a 2445/49 \u2013 2025 \u0152\u0263 \u0db8\u0dc3 17 \u0dc0\u0dd0\u01e7 \u022f\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db4\u01af\u01e6\u0daf\u0dcf \u2013 2025.07.17\n\nNo. 2445/49 \u2013 THURSDAY JULY 17, 2025\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART I: SECTION (I) \u2013 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Noti\ufb01cations\n\nL.D.B. 277/40\n\nTHE ANTIQUITIES ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 188)\n\nNoti\ufb01cation under Section 33\n\nBY virtue of the powers vested in me by Section 33 of the Antiquities Ordinance (Chapter 188), I, Delath Thusitha Mendis, Director General of Archaeology, do by this noti\ufb01cation declare with the approval of the Land Commissioner, that the area of the state land speci\ufb01ed in the Schedule, to this Noti\ufb01cation shall be an \u201cArchaeological Reserve\u201d for the purposes of the aforesaid Ordinance. DELATH THUSITHA MENDIS, Director General of Archaeology.Colombo,08th July, 2025.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nArea Reserved for Archaeological purposes of Kadawathgama Rajapihilla\n\nAll that allotment of land depicted as Lot \u2018A\u2019 in the Surveyor General\u2019s Tracing No. Maha/YIN/2023/605 dated 20.10.2023, of the land called as \u201cKadawathgama Rajapihilla\u201d situated in the village of Kadawathgama in the Grama Niladhari Division No. 204 of Kadawathgama, Central Province Korale (Yatinuwara) in the Divisional Secretary\u2019s Division of Yatinuwara, Kandy District, Central Province bounded as follows and which the said allotments of land containing in extent of Seven Decimal Twelve Perches (7.12 Perches) alias Naught Demial Naught One Eight Naught (0.0180 Hectare) is bounded as follows:\n\nNorth : Lee Magaskotuwa Home Garden of Herath Ranasinghe;East : Home Garden of Herath Ranasinghe and Lot C;South : Footpath and Lot C; West : Footpath and Stream.\n\n1A \u2013 G 044880 \u2013 05 (07/2025)\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk"
